      "writtenOn": "2020-11-25T08:22:22Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "because the libraryDecorator receiver makes the `library.buildStubs()` on L645 (right-hand side) to actually be `ctx.Module().(*Module).library.(*libraryDecoratorExtendedType).libraryDecorator.buildStubs()`, when `ctx.Module().(*Module).library` is a type extending libraryDecorator, for example llndkStubDecorator.\nHowever what we want here is actually `ctx.Module().(*Module).library.buildStubs()`. We want the methods that are provided by the libraryInterface. for example llndkStubDecorator overrides libraryInterface.buildStubs().\n\nThe receiver can be kept, but then we would have \"library\" (type *libraryDecorator, from receiver) and \"m.library\" (type *libraryInterface, from ctx) in the function body at the same time, which I think is very confusing. Since the library receiver is actually just \"m.library.(*libraryDecorator)\" or \"m.library.(*libraryDecoratorExtendedType).libraryDecorator\", I just removed the receiver.",
      "parentUuid": "710138c2_8d94686d",
